<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmmyprop1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 3.1 Quantization with Bias Awareness ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Fair-GPTQ: Bias-Aware Quantization for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We recall that the aim is to solve the Problem (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.1 Quantization with Bias Awareness ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Fair-GPTQ: Bias-Aware Quantization for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) column by column.
Before providing the proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmmyprop1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 3.1 Quantization with Bias Awareness ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Fair-GPTQ: Bias-Aware Quantization for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we first restate the Optimization Problem (<a href="#S3.Ex4" title="In 3.1 Quantization with Bias Awareness ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Fair-GPTQ: Bias-Aware Quantization for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) where the aim is to find the optimal modification <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math> to apply to the flattened version <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\Delta\mathbf{w}}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></munder><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\Delta\mathbf{w}}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\Delta\mathbf{w}+\tfrac{1}{2}\Delta\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}\Delta\mathbf{w}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\Delta\mathbf{w}+\tfrac{1}{2}\Delta\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}\Delta\mathbf{w},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\Delta\mathbf{w}=\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-w_{q}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>quant</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\Delta\mathbf{w}=\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-w_{q},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> are the first and second order derivative respectively of the flattened version of the objective function defined in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.1 Quantization with Bias Awareness ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Fair-GPTQ: Bias-Aware Quantization for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmmyprop2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_myprop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmmyprop2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmmyprop2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Weight updates and their impact)<span id="Thmmyprop2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmmyprop2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmmyprop2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmmyprop2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let us consider the optimization problem defined by Eq. (<a href="#S3.Ex4" title="In 3.1 Quantization with Bias Awareness ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Fair-GPTQ: Bias-Aware Quantization for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)
The optimal weight modification <math id="Thmmyprop2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{w}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{w}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> to apply to <math id="Thmmyprop2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmmyprop2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{w}^{\star}=-\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}-\dfrac{w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}}{[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{e}_{q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>quant</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{w}^{\star}=-\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}-\dfrac{w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}}{[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{e}_{q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmmyprop2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmmyprop2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmmyprop2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and the saliency associated to the modification is given by:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmmyprop2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f=\dfrac{(w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}})^{2}}{2[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}-\dfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>quant</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f=\dfrac{(w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}})^{2}}{2[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}-\dfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start from the Lagrangian of the optimization problem:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\Delta\mathbf{w},\lambda)=\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\Delta\mathbf{w}+\dfrac{1}{2}\Delta\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}\Delta\mathbf{w}+\lambda\left(\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\Delta\mathbf{w}+w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>quant</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\Delta\mathbf{w},\lambda)=\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\Delta\mathbf{w}+\dfrac{1}{2}\Delta\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}\Delta\mathbf{w}+\lambda\left(\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\Delta\mathbf{w}+w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We will first express the change of the weights with respect to <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, </span><span id="A1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span><span id="A1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text">, the Lagrange multiplier using its first order derivative </span><span id="A1.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">w.r.t.</span><span id="A1.p6.1.5" class="ltx_text"> to <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.
More formally, we will compute <math id="A1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dfrac{\partial L}{\partial\Delta\mathbf{w}}(\Delta\mathbf{w},\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dfrac{\partial L}{\partial\Delta\mathbf{w}}(\Delta\mathbf{w},\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and study which change in <math id="A1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math> leads to the minimum value of the Lagrangian.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial L}{\partial\Delta\mathbf{w}}(\Delta\mathbf{w},\lambda)=\mathbf{0}\iff" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial L}{\partial\Delta\mathbf{w}}(\Delta\mathbf{w},\lambda)=\mathbf{0}\iff</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}\Delta\mathbf{w}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}+\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}=\mathbf{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}\Delta\mathbf{w}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}+\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}=\mathbf{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\Delta\mathbf{w}=-\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\left(\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\Delta\mathbf{w}=-\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\left(\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can now express the Lagrangian with respect to <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> only.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\lambda)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\lambda)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\dfrac{1}{2}\left(\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\left(\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}\right)\right)^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}\left(\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\left(\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}\right)\right)-\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\left(\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\left(\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\dfrac{1}{2}\left(\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\left(\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}\right)\right)^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}\left(\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\left(\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}\right)\right)-\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\left(\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\left(\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
