<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can now rewrite the Lagrangian can be rewritten as</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\lambda)=-\dfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}-\lambda(\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}-(w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})))-\dfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>quant</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\lambda)=-\dfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}-\lambda(\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}-(w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})))-\dfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}]_{qq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}]_{qq}</annotation></semantics></math> designates the <math id="A1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-th element on the diagonal of the <math id="A1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> matrix.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">We compute the derivative of the Lagrangian in order to find the optimal value <math id="A1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for which the Lagrangian reaches its maximum.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial L}{\partial\lambda}(\lambda)=0\iff" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial L}{\partial\lambda}(\lambda)=0\iff</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;-\lambda[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}+w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>quant</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;-\lambda[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}+w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\lambda=\dfrac{w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}}{[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>quant</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\lambda=\dfrac{w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}}{[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, we also know that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}\Delta\mathbf{w}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}+\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}=\mathbf{0}\iff\Delta\mathbf{w}=-\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}(\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}+\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}\Delta\mathbf{w}+\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}+\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}=\mathbf{0}\iff\Delta\mathbf{w}=-\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}(\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}+\lambda\mathbf{e}_{q}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">We finally have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\Delta\mathbf{w}=-\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}-\dfrac{w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}}{[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{e}_{q}.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>quant</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\Delta\mathbf{w}=-\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}-\dfrac{w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}}{[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{e}_{q}.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to study the change in loss occurred when we update <math id="A1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> with the expression (<a href="#A1.E8" title="In Proposition 2 (Weight updates and their impact). ‣ Appendix A Proof of Proposition ‣ Fair-GPTQ: Bias-Aware Quantization for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) of <math id="A1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This change is equal to:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{q}=-\dfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}-\lambda(\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}-(w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})))-\dfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>quant</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{q}=-\dfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}-\lambda(\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}-(w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})))-\dfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\dfrac{w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}}{[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>quant</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\dfrac{w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}}{[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">This last expression can be simplified as follows:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{L_{q}=\dfrac{(w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}})^{2}}{2[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}-\dfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}=\Delta f.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>quant</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐉</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{L_{q}=\dfrac{(w_{q}-\operatorname{quant}(w_{q})-\mathbf{e}_{q}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}})^{2}}{2[\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}]_{qq}}-\dfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{w}}^{-1}\mathbf{J}_{\mathbf{w}}=\Delta f.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Benchmark Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix, we provide a summary of the benchmarks used for evaluation.
For all the benchmarks, we utilize the official implementation unless explicitly stated otherwise. To assess perplexity, we employ the implementation provided by the Transformers’ Evaluate library<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
            
            
            
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/spaces/evaluate-metric/perplexity" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/spaces/evaluate-metric/perplexity</a></span></span></span>, based on the standard perplexity metric proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jelinek et al. [1977]</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Zero-Shot Benchmarks</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For zero-shot benchmarks, we rely on the implementations provided by the LM Evaluation Harness framework.<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness</a></span></span></span> The reported accuracy metrics specifically refer to accuracy computed based on the likelihood of the model’s generated answers. Additionally, we include random baselines for comparison in Table <a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ B.1 Zero-Shot Benchmarks ‣ Appendix B Benchmark Details ‣ Fair-GPTQ: Bias-Aware Quantization for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
