<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Zero-shot evaluation results of OPT models with Fair-GPTQ, corresponding to the application of Fair-GPTQ debiasing on all layers on attention output and output fully connected matrices with (<math id="A4.T7.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>) for <math id="A4.T7.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ALL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ALL</annotation></semantics></math> strategy and <math id="A4.T7.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> for the rest.
<span id="A4.T7.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">All</span> applies debiasing to all layers; <span id="A4.T7.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">lower</span> and <span id="A4.T7.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">upper</span> apply it to the bottom and top 10% of layers, respectively; <span id="A4.T7.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">UL</span> applies it to 5% of each. PPL = WikiText-2 perplexity; SS = StereoSet; CP = CrowS-Pairs. Accuracy is reported on zero-shot benchmarks (higher is better). For stereotype-bias benchmarks, a score of 50 indicates neutrality (i.e., no pro- or anti-stereotype bias).
PPL denotes perplexity on Wikitext-2.
GPTQ-C4 refers to LLMs quantized using C4 calibration data following the original source implementation.
GPTQ-SS refers to LLMs quantized using StereoSet development calibration data. </figcaption>
</figure>
